# The build options of the bitstream, one KEY=VALUE per line, no quotes, no comment after a value (U20 A7, MultiCore's form). ci/keys.sh exports
# them before it computes the key (gateware_key in ci/lib.sh puts them into it); the builder exports them before Vivado. An empty value builds the
# default of designs/c64_basic/build.tcl, as an unset variable does. The Gitea bitstream stage sets none of them, so every one is empty here and the
# key is the one the Gitea pipeline computes (tools/check_vivado_env.py holds the two together while .gitea/workflows/bitstream.yml exists).
# TRX_SID: empty = reDIP with 8 SIDs; redip2 = the two-SID reDIP
TRX_SID=
# T16_SLOT: empty = the expansion port on; 0 = idle
T16_SLOT=
# TRX_FEATURES: empty = no optional block; jtag = the JTAG debug master
TRX_FEATURES=
